  "slug": "learning-biology-small-c2ee",
  "summary": "HEDGEHOG's stage-wise filtering of 22 generators on KRAS G12D shows attrition that standard metrics miss, alongside new conditioned generators and screening pipelines.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is evaluation and application of molecular generative and screening models under explicit constraints, though not every item is a benchmark. HEDGEHOG is the clearest evaluation study: a configurable six-stage workflow applied to 22 generative models on KRAS G12D that exposes stage-wise attrition standard metrics miss. Method papers add constrained generation, including PharmaDiff (pharmacophore-conditioned 3D diffusion), PartiDesign (structure-sequence co-design across proteins, nucleic acids and small molecules) and SF-GA (redesigning predicted P-gp substrates into synthetically accessible non-substrates). Application work includes a GNN-docking-MD pipeline that identified carvedilol as a partial THRβ agonist, confirmed by TR-FRET and cell lipid assays, and a rule-defined PEG ligand library of about 50M retained structures. The new element is filtering and experimental confirmation, not architecture.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-10"
}
